From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netifd: preserve bridge-owned intra-BSS forwarding

Some AP drivers send all bridged intra-BSS traffic through Linux instead
of using an internal shortcut. Accept that explicit driver capability and
include it in the bridge hairpin decision independently of multicast
conversion or proxy-ARP policy. Isolation continues to take precedence.

Generic wireless/AP metadata does not identify this forwarding owner. Keep
the property capability-based rather than selecting a chipset in netifd.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

--- a/device.h
+++ b/device.h
@@ -321,6 +321,8 @@ struct device {
 	bool default_config;
 	bool wireless;
 	bool wireless_ap;
+	/* This driver routes all bridged intra-BSS traffic through the bridge. */
+	bool wireless_bridge_forwarding;
 	bool wireless_proxyarp;
 	bool wireless_isolate;
 	bool bpdu_filter;
--- a/system-linux.c
+++ b/system-linux.c
@@ -976,7 +976,10 @@ system_bridge_set_wireless(struct device
 	         !bridge->settings.multicast_to_unicast)
 		mcast_to_ucast = false;
 
-	hairpin = mcast_to_ucast || dev->wireless_proxyarp;
+	/* Some drivers have no intra-BSS shortcut while bridged. Preserve
+	 * same-BSS delivery independently of multicast conversion policy. */
+	hairpin = mcast_to_ucast || dev->wireless_proxyarp ||
+		  dev->wireless_bridge_forwarding;
 	if (dev->wireless_isolate)
 		hairpin = false;
 
--- a/ucode.c
+++ b/ucode.c
@@ -102,6 +102,8 @@ uc_netifd_device_set(uc_vm_t *vm, size_t
 		dev->wireless = bval;
 	if (prop_get_bool(data, "wireless_isolate", &bval))
 		dev->wireless_isolate = bval;
+	if (prop_get_bool(data, "wireless_bridge_forwarding", &bval))
+		dev->wireless_bridge_forwarding = bval;
 	if (prop_get_bool(data, "wireless_proxyarp", &bval))
 		dev->wireless_proxyarp = bval;
 	if (prop_get_bool(data, "wireless_ap", &bval)) {
